questions.text:
Identify the homoleptic complexes with odd number of d electrons in the central metal.

(A) [\text{FeO}_4]^{2-}
(B) [\text{Fe(CN)}_6]^{3-}
(C) [\text{Fe(CN)}_5\text{NO}]^{2-}
(D) [\text{CoCl}_4]^{2-}
(E) [\text{Co(H}_2\text{O)}_3\text{F}_3]

Choose the correct answer from the options given below :

If \text{C(diamond)} \rightarrow \text{C(graphite)} + \text{X kJ mol}^{-1}
\text{C(diamond)} + \text{O}_2\text{(g)} \rightarrow \text{CO}_2\text{(g)} + \text{Y kJ mol}^{-1}
\text{C(graphite)} + \text{O}_2\text{(g)} \rightarrow \text{CO}_2\text{(g)} + \text{Z kJ mol}^{-1}
at constant temperature. Then :

questions.solution:
Subtracting equation (3) from (2):
\text{C(diamond)} - \text{C(graphite)} \rightarrow (\text{Y} - \text{Z})\text{ kJ}
\text{C(diamond)} \rightarrow \text{C(graphite)} + (\text{Y} - \text{Z})\text{ kJ}
Comparing with equation (1) gives \text{X} = \text{Y} - \text{Z}.

Equation of chord with given midpoint (T = S_1):
\frac{x x_1}{9} + \frac{y y_1}{4} = \frac{x_1^2}{9} + \frac{y_1^2}{4}
\frac{5x}{18} + \frac{y}{8} = \frac{25}{36} + \frac{1}{16} = \frac{109}{144}
Multiplying by 144: 40x + 18y = 109.
Comparing with \alpha x + \beta y = 109 \implies \alpha = 40, \beta = 18.
\alpha + \beta = 40 + 18 = 58.
